  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Christopher Wuerz worked directly with public officials on bringing government services online. As CRW Systems' president, he joined the development and implementation group for Idaho's Customer Access System. The project let contractors buy permits, pay fees and request inspections without visiting an office; licensed tradespeople could also renew their credentials online.\n\nAfter the launch, users reported difficulties entering site addresses and searching the system. The building-safety agency worked with CRW to address those problems and chose a gradual introduction of online features while technical issues were corrected. It also established a helpline for customers needing assistance.",
    "html": "<p>Christopher Wuerz worked directly with public officials on bringing government services online. As CRW Systems' president, he joined the development and implementation group for Idaho's Customer Access System. The project let contractors buy permits, pay fees and request inspections without visiting an office; licensed tradespeople could also renew their credentials online.</p>\r\n<p>After the launch, users reported difficulties entering site addresses and searching the system. The building-safety agency worked with CRW to address those problems and chose a gradual introduction of online features while technical issues were corrected. It also established a helpline for customers needing assistance.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 96,
    "confidence": {
      "score": 86,
